report=['# LLPS spatial niche clustering v1', '', '**Analysis scope: LLPS only. C5-associated transcriptional signal is not validated C5 CAF abundance; LLPS-associated activity is not physical phase separation.**','',
'## 1. Included material',f'{d.section_id.nunique()} sections; {len(d):,} spots; {d.dataset.nunique()} source groups (some source identities remain UNVERIFIED). {d.patient_uid.nunique()} confirmed patients across {d[d.patient_uid.notna()].section_id.nunique()} sections. No inferred patient identities or stages. All audited spots retained.',
'## 2. R1/R2/R3',table(sizes.groupby('radius').agg(mean_size=('mean','mean'),mean_median=('median','mean'),min_size=('min','min'),max_size=('max','max')).reset_index()),table(coverage.groupby('radius').mean(numeric_only=True).reset_index()),f'Exact array offsets ensure no cross-section edges or interpolation. Squidpy grid discrepancies: {graphs.squidpy_extra_directed_edges.sum()} extra and {graphs.squidpy_missing_directed_edges.sum()} missing directed edges corrected to exact array adjacency. R2/R3 use graph-reachable cumulative neighborhoods, counting centers once. Larger radius averages more tissue and increases smoothing.',
'## 3. Continuous abundance versus dominant-type native method',table(rd('03_clustering/native_quality_metrics.tsv')),table(rd('03_clustering/native_quantization_audit.tsv')),'The native dominant-type control produces hundreds of clusters in these fixed settings. This is severe overpartitioning; high silhouette in a discrete composition space is not evidence of superior ecological validity. Repeated quantized profiles and KNN ties are diagnosed explicitly. It is not recommended as a biological niche taxonomy.',table(native[native.model_b.str.startswith('native_')&native.model_a.isin(['recommended_niche','major_best_niche','subtype_best_niche'])]),'Native Squidpy1.6.5 runs on pooled all-spot dominant composition with scale=False; main method is continuous section-balanced training plus unified mapping. Thus comparison includes training-balance and representation differences. Native cumulative binary radius graphs supplied at distance1 avoid multiple path weighting. The installed1.6.5 missing-neighbor padding bug is corrected with sparse profile counts, validated on a toy and all input profiles. Mixing loss is quantified in dominant_information_loss.tsv.',
'## 4–5. Niche counts and recommendation',table(rec[['role','model','n_niches','silhouette','min_fraction','selection_score']]),'The best model means best among evaluated candidates, not an exhaustive optimum. Recommendation fixed using composition-only silhouette with prespecified tiny/overfragmented-cluster penalties. No signature, clinical variable, communications or spatial coordinate entered selection. See model_selection_report.md for exact staged search and mapping. Candidate quality indexes, full pooled validation and low-confidence mappings are retained. Seed stability isolates Leiden randomness on a fixed pilot and fixed KNN, not repeated biological sampling.',table(rd('03_clustering/label_transfer_confidence.tsv').groupby('model').agg(section_balanced_mean_confidence=('mean_confidence','mean'),section_balanced_low_confidence_fraction=('below_0_6','mean')).reset_index()),table(st.groupby('model').agg(min_ARI=('ARI','min'),mean_ARI=('ARI','mean'),min_NMI=('NMI','min')).reset_index()),table(ari[ari.scope=='all_spots_balanced_vs_pooled']),table(rd('03_clustering/convergence_diagnostic.tsv')),
'## 6. Biological characterization',table(names),'Names are descriptive of section-balanced central composition. Separate central/neighborhood and pooled/section/patient-balanced tables prevent presenting only the clustering input. No label is evidence of malignant status or a functional mechanism.',
'## 7. Dataset effect',table(bias[bias.model=='recommended_niche']),'Dataset and section dominance are descriptive warnings, not proof of a removable technical batch. No Harmony or forced mixing used. Known original subtype identifiability limits remain relevant to subtype niches.',
'## 8. Fragmentation and smoothing',table(frag.groupby('model').agg(mean_singleton_fraction=('singleton_fraction','mean'),mean_largest_fraction=('largest_fraction','mean'),mean_same_label_edges=('same_label_edge_fraction','mean')).reset_index()),'Spatial continuity is auxiliary: averaging itself induces it. Original missing tissue and disconnected tissue islands also contribute to fragmentation. Connected-component size distributions and all-section maps must be visually reviewed for boundary merging; automated metrics cannot exclude over-smoothing.',
'## 9–10. C5 and LLPS enrichment', 'Verified-patient paired contrasts (within-section z, min20 per niche and rest; then same-patient mean):',table(base[['niche','feature','n_units','effect','ci_low','ci_high','FDR','positive_fraction']]),'All-section sensitivity (sections are not guaranteed independent patients):',table(sectionbase[['niche','feature','n_units','effect','ci_low','ci_high','FDR','positive_fraction']]),'Raw-score and percentile results, min10/20/30 and fibroblast P50/P75/P90 subsets remain in full tables; no significant-only filtering.',
'## 11. Fibroblast adjustment',table(adjusted[adjusted.unit=='patient'][['niche','feature','n_units','effect','ci_low','ci_high','FDR','positive_fraction']]),'Section-specific shared-support regression controls log absolute and relative Fibroblast abundance with quadratic terms. Low support or ill-conditioning returns NA; residual plots alone are not adjusted niche-effect tests. Exact eligibility and all failures are in niche_fibroblast_adjusted_results.tsv. Adjustment is associational, with remaining tissue/technical confounding.',table(rd('05_C5_LLPS_enrichment/niche_signature_overlap_audit.tsv')),
'## 12. Joint C5–LLPS–Endothelial niche',table(joint_sensitivity),'C5 unadjusted enrichment is partition-dependent: R2/R3, subtype and Kmeans controls can contain positive niches despite the negative primary screen. Across all five continuous models, no positive verified-patient C5 adjusted contrast passes the stated BH/CI screen, whereas LLPS adjusted positives recur. R3 has an unadjusted C5/Endothelial pair-only pattern; none of the eight fixed models has a triple-positive pattern. This distinction prevents calling every C5-associated pattern absent based only on the main taxonomy.',table(sensitivity),f'Under the explicit descriptive screen of positive verified-patient effects, nominal95%CI above0 and BH FDR<0.05 for all three within-section standardized features, jointly supported niche IDs are {sorted(joint)}. C5–Endothelial pair-only supported IDs: {sorted(joint_C5_Endo)}. Fibroblast and Endothelial composition helped define niches, so their enrichment is partly definitional rather than independent evidence. This screen is not an independent confirmatory joint test and does not establish a fibrovascular mechanism. Absence of qualifying niches is a negative result for this screen, not proof of absence.',
'## 13. Across-section and source reproducibility','Per-section Pearson and Spearman correlations are saved for center and neighborhood scales, each niche and whole section, before/after Fibroblast adjustment. Fisher-z mean correlations and bootstrap section/patient intervals use biological-unit aggregation. Dataset-specific direction summaries retain heterogeneity; section and patient inference do not cover identical source populations.',table(rd('06_C5_endothelial/correlation_summary.tsv').query("niche == 'ALL' and scale == 'center' and method == 'pearson' and unit == 'patient'")[['feature_a','feature_b','adjustment','n_units','r','ci_low','ci_high','positive_fraction']]),
'Additional source sensitivity for adjusted LLPS in main Niche1:',table(rd('05_C5_LLPS_enrichment/adjusted_dataset_summary.tsv').query("niche == 1 and feature == 'LLPS77_UCell'")),'GSE285715 has weaker/mixed adjusted directions and unresolved patient identities. Reused LLPS77 scores also have source-specific gene coverage; within-section normalization does not recover absent genes.',table(rd('00_input_audit/LLPS77_gene_coverage.tsv').groupby('dataset').agg(min_genes=('covered','min'),max_genes=('covered','max'),n_sections=('section_id','size')).reset_index()),'## 14. Niche adjacency','R1,1000 within-section label permutations,seed123. Observed, expected,SD,Z,O/E saved for every section; absent pairs and zero-variance Z are NA. Section/patient/source summaries prioritize O/E and direction. Spatially defined niches inherently autocorrelate, so these maps describe organization and cannot independently demonstrate cell communication.',
'## 15. Clinical associations',table(rd('08_clinical_association/clinical_sample_sizes.tsv')),table(rd('08_clinical_association/stage_sample_sizes.tsv')),'Original workbook re-audit recovered explicit T stages for7 exact-accession sections (GSE171351:T2 three,T3 one; GSE285715:T3 two,T4 one with unknown patients). Within-dataset independent groups are too small for reliable stage inference; descriptive tables retained.','Verified labels only; dataset-stratified description. Formal tests require >=5 known independent patients in both groups. Compositional closure prevents treating niche fractions as independent outcomes. No new stage inference or unsupported compositional modeling.',f'Eligible nominal tests: {clinical.p.notna().sum()}; rows without sufficient verified groups remain descriptive.',
'## 16. Figure candidates','Recommended: section-balanced central composition; major/subtype UMAP with source QC; score-blind representative spatial maps; patient/section contrasts with confidence intervals; O/E summary heatmap. Representative sections selected by niche diversity per source then coverage, never by C5/LLPS. Additional Kmeans/R2/R3 and native-control spatial QC maps use these same representatives; native previews color only the five largest groups and label the rest as pooled other clusters. All63 spatial outputs retained. UMAP plotting samples50000 spots only for readability; full embeddings and labels saved.',
'## 17. Negative, unstable or unidentifiable findings','K-means K5 has much higher seed stability than the finer Leiden taxonomy. It should be reviewed as a coarser alternative, not treated as confirmation of identical niche boundaries. Native dominant profiles overpartition into hundreds of groups and are not a credible standalone niche taxonomy here. Subtype silhouette is negative for the retained candidate; fine subtype niche identities are especially uncertain.','Report all negative contrasts, zero/low signature values, low-support adjusted comparisons, mapping uncertainty, cross-scale disagreement, source-dominated niches and unresolved clinical groups. Known C5 specificity limitations prohibit C5 cell-localization claims. Unverified cohorts and only29 verified patients limit generalization. No iid spot-level significance is used.',
'## 18. Next steps','Within the frozen main taxonomy, prioritize Niche1 for independent LLPS-associated transcriptional validation (mixed central composition with relatively prominent Mural cells); its C5-associated signal is not a supported positive adjusted effect. Niche6 is an Endothelial-enriched comparison region, not an established C5/LLPS fibrovascular niche; source imbalance must be checked. Niche7 has a strong Mural component but too few verified patients for strong claims. Do not equate reference Matrix_CAF or other CAF subtypes with validated C5 cells.','After manual spatial/histology review, prioritize reproducible composition niches with adequate cross-source and patient support. Consider targeted expression or spatial validation separating fibroblast abundance from transcriptional state. Niche DEG/pseudobulk, GO/KEGG/GSEA, CellChat and NicheNet were intentionally not run in this round.',
'## Evidence decisions',table(pd.DataFrame(ratings)),'Overall: **CONDITIONAL GO for exploratory spatial organization**, contingent on histological review, subtype identifiability and mapping/balance stability. A negative C5/Endothelial hypothesis does not invalidate spatial niche analysis.',
'## Reproducibility and limits','4-core CPU affinity; numerical thread caps4; address-space limit100GB. Seed123 except seed-stability checks. Exact input IDs, composition and graph QC, scripts, frozen software and per-stage resource logs retained. Original inputs read-only; no expression matrix or full H&E copied. Environment and figures are excluded from biological inference. See logs for dependency compatibility fixes and any actual execution failures; outputs must pass final_validation.json before delivery.']
